<title>PERU: Peru loses 1.4 million man-hours in 1996 strikes.</title>
<headline>Peru loses 1.4 million man-hours in 1996 strikes.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru lost 1.40 million man-hours in 77 private sector strikes during 1996, up from 1.05 million man-hours lost during 102 strikes in 1995, the Labor Ministry said Tuesday.</p>
<p>In December last year, the country lost only 6,000 man- hours in three strikes, compared with 94,000 man-hours in six strikes in the same month in 1995, the ministry said in its monthly report.</p>
<p>The total of man-hours lost in strikes in Peru has fallen dramatically from the 15.068 million man-hours lost in 1990, when President Alberto Fujimori's government took power.</p>
<p>((-- Saul Hudson, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134))</p>
